# graphify: keep the graph about application/library CODE only.
# git-style patterns, honored by BOTH `graphify extract` and the pre-commit `graphify update`.
# `--code-only` on extract is NOT enough on its own — `update` rejects that flag and re-adds
# these on the next commit, so this ignore file is the update-safe lever.

# docs, plans, ADRs, instruction files (CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md), skill prose
*.md

# design studies and everything else under docs/ (HTML too — not app code)
docs/

# agent / editor / CI config — not application code
.claude/
.husky/
.github/
.agents/

# repo tooling and agent-facing skill definitions
scripts/
packages/argo-skills/

# the Electron cockpit is deprecated — apps/macOS is the app the graph is about.
# Left in, its ~2.5k TS nodes swamped the Swift tree to 27 nodes of noise.
apps/desktop/

# Xcode project metadata and asset catalogues — build config, not application code
*.xcodeproj/
*.xcassets/
